ef 1080 "⟨0,0,0⟩" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488922 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488922 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "d9d9f5c3-101a-532e-8e93-6d12cddd64ee" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489088 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186488485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489088 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186488669 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489088 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186488681 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489088 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186488874 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489088 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186488922 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489088 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489088 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489088 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186488669 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489088 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "87266618-2882-52b8-96d1-51f6b11cd2c6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489106 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186488541 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489106 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186488639 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489106 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186488769 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489106 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186488862 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489106 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186488894 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489106 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489106 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489106 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186488639 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489106 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "a2e1827e-bb95-5b76-9c80-da8e23a83f9e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489135 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186488533 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489135 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186488598 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489135 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186488660 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489135 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186488671 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489135 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186488891 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489135 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489135 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489135 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186488598 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489135 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "cee411fe-3c0d-5c7d-9c42-5d9b1df29d7b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489198 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186489135 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489198 #edb/ref 1069 "q-105956" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489198 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489198 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨z,\\sqrt{x},0⟩$ and the scalar field $f(x,y,z)=-z.$ Given that\n\n$$\n∇\\times F=⟨0,1,\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}}⟩,\\,∇f=⟨0,0,-1⟩,\n$$\n\ncalculate $∇\\times (f\\,F)$ at the point $(4,1,4).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489198 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2c76b758-88c8-5667-93d2-dbb6a9e1da40" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489198 #edb/ref 1074 "We shall use the following identity:\n\n$$\n∇\\times (f\\,F)=f∇\\times F+∇f\\times F\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute $∇f\\times F.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f\\times F & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ z & \\sqrt{x} & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =[0(0)-(-1)(\\sqrt{x})]i-[0(0)-(-1)(z)]j+[0(\\sqrt{x})-0(z)]k \\\\  & =\\sqrt{x}\\,i-z\\,j+0\\,k \\\\  & =⟨\\sqrt{x},-z,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (f\\,F) & =f∇\\times F+∇f\\times F \\\\  & =(-z)⟨0,1,\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}}⟩+⟨\\sqrt{x},-z,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,-z,-\\frac{z}{2\\sqrt{x}}⟩+⟨\\sqrt{x},-z,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\sqrt{x},-2z,-\\frac{z}{2\\sqrt{x}}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (f\\,F)(4,1,4) & =⟨\\sqrt{4},-2(4),-\\frac{4}{2\\sqrt{4}}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,-8,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489265 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186489106 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489265 #edb/ref 1069 "q-105791" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489265 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489265 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate $∇\\times (4F+G)$ at the point $(0,1,-1)$ for the vector fields $F$ and $G,$ where\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=y{e}^{x}\\,i+xz\\,j+(y-1)\\,\\text{k},\\,(∇\\times G)(x,y,z)=z\\,i.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489265 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c8edc0c0-9a3d-5546-8149-aa1e5f0446b7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489265 #edb/ref 1074 "If $F$ and $G$ are vector fields and $k$ is a constant, then we have the following linearity properties for curl:\n\n- $∇\\times (kF)=k∇\\times F$\n\n- $∇\\times (F+G)=∇\\times F+∇\\times G$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (4F+G) & =∇\\times (4F)+∇\\times G \\\\  & =4∇\\times F+∇\\times G.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to calculate $∇\\times F.$ In doing so, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times F & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x} & \\frac{∂}{∂y} & \\frac{∂}{∂z} \\\\ y{e}^{x} & xz & y-1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =[\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y-1)-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(xz)]i-[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(y-1)-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(y{e}^{x})]j+[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(xz)-\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y{e}^{x})]k \\\\  & =(1-x)\\,i-(0-0)\\,j+(z-{e}^{x})\\,k \\\\  & =(1-x)\\,i+(z-{e}^{x})\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the linearity properties, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (4F+G) & =4(∇\\times F)+∇\\times G \\\\  & =4[(1-x)\\,i+(z-{e}^{x})\\,k]+z\\,i \\\\  & =4(1-x)\\,i+4(z-{e}^{x})\\,k+z\\,i \\\\  & =[4(1-x)+z]\\,i+4(z-{e}^{x})\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating at the point $(0,1,-1),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(∇\\times (4F+G))(0,1,-1) & =[4(1-0)+(-1)]\\,i+4(-1-{e}^{0})\\,k \\\\  & =[4-1]\\,i+4(-1-1)\\,k \\\\  & =3\\,i-8\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489290 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186489088 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489290 #edb/ref 1069 "q-105897" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489290 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489290 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨x{e}^{y},z,0⟩$ and the scalar field $f(x,y,z)=x-{e}^{y}.$ Given that\n\n$$\n∇\\times F=⟨-1,0,-x{e}^{y}⟩,\\,∇f=⟨1,-{e}^{y},0⟩,\n$$\n\ncalculate $∇\\times (f\\,F)$ at the point $(2,0,-3).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489290 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f311fcaa-7f7c-50da-9066-652f1bc7fb5e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489290 #edb/ref 1074 "We shall use the following identity:\n\n$$\n∇\\times (f\\,F)=f∇\\times F+∇f\\times F\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute $∇f\\times F.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f\\times F & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & -{e}^{y} & 0 \\\\ x{e}^{y} & z & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =[-{e}^{y}(0)-0(z)]i-[1(0)-0(x{e}^{y})]j+[1(z)-(-{e}^{y})(x{e}^{y})]k \\\\  & =0\\,i-0\\,j+(z+x{e}^{2y})\\,k \\\\  & =⟨0,0,z+x{e}^{2y}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (f\\,F) & =f∇\\times F+∇f\\times F \\\\  & =(x-{e}^{y})⟨-1,0,-x{e}^{y}⟩+⟨0,0,z+x{e}^{2y}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{e}^{y}-x,0,x{e}^{2y}-{x}^{2}{e}^{y}⟩+⟨0,0,z+x{e}^{2y}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{e}^{y}-x,0,2x{e}^{2y}+z-{x}^{2}{e}^{y}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (f\\,F)(2,0,-3) & =⟨{e}^{0}-2,0,2(2){e}^{2(0)}+(-3)-(2)^{2}{e}^{0}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,0,-3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
